      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, but isn't saying the \"cost of inertia exceeds the cost of transition\" basically just dismissing the very real suffering of people who can't afford heating or electricity right now? it feels like you're saying climate goals are more important than people's actual livelihoods. isn't that kind of a biased way to look at it?",
